TITLE:: SFPlayerMeterView
summary:: A GUI widget that displays SFPlayer input levels and server output levels
categories:: GUI>Views
related:: Classes/ScopeView, Classes/FreqScopeView, Classes/ServerMeter, Classes/ServerMeter2View

DESCRIPTION::
A link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView:: is a unified widget that combines link::Classes/ServerMeter2View:: for output monitoring with custom input meters for SFPlayer audio. It uses a hybrid approach: ServerMeter2View handles server outputs while custom LevelIndicator widgets monitor a specific player bus. This allows you to monitor the actual audio from SFPlayer rather than line inputs.

note::
If you are looking for a quick input/output levels display without having to build your own GUI from scratch, see link::Classes/SFPlayerMeter:: and link::Classes/Server#-meter::
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: height
Get the height in pixels of the standard link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView:: widget

returns:: an link::Classes/Integer::

METHOD:: getWidth
Get the width in pixels of a link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView:: widget with the given number of inputs and outputs

ARGUMENT:: numIns
number of inputs used to calculate the width

ARGUMENT:: numOuts
number of outputs used to calculate the width

ARGUMENT:: server
the server

returns:: an link::Classes/Integer::

METHOD:: new
Create a new link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView:: instance

ARGUMENT:: aserver
The link::Classes/Server:: whose outputs will be monitored

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent link::Classes/View:: or link::Classes/Window:: where the new link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView:: will be embedded.

ARGUMENT:: leftUp
Where to position the new link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView:: inside the parent. strong::leftUp:: must be a link::Classes/Point::, describing where to place the upper left corner of the new link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView::.

ARGUMENT:: numIns
The number of inputs to monitor (typically 2 for stereo player audio)

ARGUMENT:: numOuts
The number of outputs to monitor

ARGUMENT:: playerBus
The link::Classes/Bus:: where SFPlayer outputs its audio

returns:: A new link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView::

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: playerBus
get the link::Classes/Bus:: that is being monitored for input levels

returns:: a link::Classes/Bus::

METHOD:: remove
Removes the meter from its parent view and cleans up all associated resources including the output meter, custom input meters, monitoring synth, and OSC responder.

returns:: this link::Classes/SFPlayerMeterView::

PRIVATE:: init

EXAMPLES::

subsection::Simple Usage

code::
// Create a player bus and SFPlayer
~playerBus = Bus.audio(s, 2);
~sfp = SFPlayer.new("path/to/audio.wav", outbus: ~playerBus.index);

// Create a parent view for the meter
~meterContainer = View.new(Rect(0, 0, 300, 200));

// Create unified meter (handles both input and output monitoring)
~meter = SFPlayerMeterView.new(s, ~meterContainer, 0@0, 2, 2, ~playerBus);
::

subsection::Integration with SFPlayer

code::
// Set up SFPlayer with custom bus
~playerBus = Bus.audio(s, 2);
~sfp = SFPlayer.new("path/to/audio.wav", outbus: ~playerBus.index, loop: true);

// Create meter container in your main GUI
~meterContainer = View.new(Rect(180, 107, 320, 275)).background_(Color.black);

// Create unified meter to monitor player audio and server outputs
~meter = SFPlayerMeterView.new(s, ~meterContainer, 68@0, 2, 4, ~playerBus);

// Start playback
~sfp.play;
::
